/-!
# Hamiltonians of a diffeotopy on the manifold

Let `σ` be a two-form on a manifold `M` and `φ_t`, `t ∈ [0, 1]`, a smooth diffeotopy of `M` with
velocity `X_t` (`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.velocity`). In McDuff–Salamon, §3.1, `φ_t` is generated by a
time-dependent Hamiltonian `H : M × [0, 1] → ℝ` when `ι_{X_t} σ = dH_t` for every `t`
(`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsGeneratedBy`). Tau Ceti's `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian` reads the
same Hamiltonian along the motion, as `F_t = H_t ∘ φ_t`. This file relates the two readings and
transports Tau Ceti's rules for composites, inverses and conjugates to the reading on `M`. It
also shows that a diffeotopy has a Hamiltonian as soon as every `ι_{X_t} σ` is exact.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsGeneratedBy σ Φ G`: `G` is smooth and `ι_{X_t} σ = dG_t` for every `t`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.hasHamiltonian_iff_contMDiff_and_isHamiltonianVectorField_velocity`: `F` is
  a Hamiltonian read along the motion exactly when it is smooth and `F_t ∘ φ_t⁻¹` has Hamiltonian
  vector field `X_t` for every `t`.
* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.hasHamiltonian_comp_iff`: `(x, t) ↦ G (φ_t x, t)` is a Hamiltonian read along
  the motion exactly when `G` generates `φ_t`.
* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsGeneratedBy.trans`, `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsGeneratedBy.symm`,
  `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsGeneratedBy.transDiffeomorph`: if `F` generates `φ_t` and `G` generates
  `ψ_t`, then `F_t + G_t ∘ φ_t⁻¹` generates `φ_t ∘ ψ_t` (when every `φ_t` preserves `σ`),
  `-F_t ∘ φ_t` generates `φ_t⁻¹` (when every `φ_t` preserves `σ`), and `F_t ∘ χ` generates
  `χ⁻¹ ∘ φ_t ∘ χ` (when `χ` preserves `σ`).
* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsGeneratedBy.timeSlice_mem_diffeomorphStabilizer`,
  `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian.timeSlice_mem_diffeomorphStabilizer`,
  `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsGeneratedBy.isHamiltonian`: for a closed `σ` on a manifold without
  boundary, the maps of a diffeotopy generated by a function on `M × [0, 1]`, or with a
  Hamiltonian read along the motion, preserve `σ`, so such a diffeotopy is Hamiltonian.
* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian.exists_sub_eq`,
  `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsGeneratedBy.exists_sub_eq`: two Hamiltonians of the same diffeotopy, in
  either reading, differ on every connected component of `M` by a smooth function of `t` alone.
* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.exists_hasHamiltonian_iff_forall_interiorₗ_velocity_mem_exactForms`: a
  diffeotopy has a Hamiltonian, read along the motion, exactly when every `ι_{X_t} σ` is exact.
  This is Tau Ceti's `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.exists_hasHamiltonian_iff` with exactness in place of a
  Hamiltonian function at each time. The Hamiltonian is built by
  `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.exists_hasHamiltonian_of_forall_mem_exactForms`, from a primitive of each
  `ι_{X_t} σ` (`TauCeti.exists_contMDiff_mextDeriv_eq_of_mem_exactForms`), and Tau Ceti's theorem
  makes the choice jointly smooth.
* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.isHamiltonian_iff_forall_interiorₗ_velocity_mem_exactForms`: a diffeotopy
  whose slices preserve `σ` is Hamiltonian exactly when every `ι_{X_t} σ` is exact.
* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsHamiltonian.interiorₗ_velocity_mem_exactForms`,
  `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsHamiltonian.pathIntegral_interiorₗ_velocity_eq_zero`: for a Hamiltonian
  diffeotopy every `ι_{X_t} σ` is exact, so its line integral along a closed `C¹` curve vanishes.
* `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.flux_congr`: equal diffeotopies have equal fluxes, whatever proofs that
  their final maps preserve the closed form are given.

## Implementation notes

In Lean the composite `φ_t ∘ ψ_t` is `Ψ.trans Φ`, and the conjugate `χ⁻¹ ∘ φ_t ∘ χ` is
`Φ.transDiffeomorph χ.symm`. The three rules are Tau Ceti's
`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian.trans`, `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian.symm` and
`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian.transDiffeomorph`, translated by `hasHamiltonian_comp_iff`.
The two readings are compared through Tau Ceti's
`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.hasHamiltonian_iff_isHamiltonianVectorField_velocity`, which assumes the
reading on `M` smooth, and `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian.isHamiltonianVectorField_velocity`.

## References

* [D. McDuff and D. Salamon, *Introduction to Symplectic Topology*][McDuffSalamon2017], §3.1,
  Definition 3.1.13 (Hamiltonian isotopies),
  Exercise 3.1.14 and Remark 3.1.15.
-/

public noncomputable section

open Set
open scoped Manifold ContDiff

namespace TauCeti.Diffeotopy

variable {E H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [TopologicalSpace H]
  {J : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H} {M : Type*} [TopologicalSpace M] [ChartedSpace H M]

variable [IsManifold J ∞ M] {σ : SmoothTwoForm J M} {Φ Ψ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M}
  {F G : M × unitInterval → ℝ}

/-- A function `G` on `M × [0, 1]` **generates** the diffeotopy `φ_t` for the two-form `σ` when it
is smooth and, for every `t`, the velocity `X_t` of `φ_t` is a Hamiltonian vector field of
`G_t = G (·, t)`, that is `ι_{X_t} σ = dG_t`. This is the time-dependent Hamiltonian read on `M`;
Tau Ceti's `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.HasHamiltonian` reads it along the motion
(`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.hasHamiltonian_comp_iff`). -/
def IsGeneratedBy (σ : SmoothTwoForm J M) (Φ : Diffeotopy J ∞ M) (G : M × unitInterval → ℝ) :
    Prop :=
  ContMDiff (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ G ∧
    ∀ t, σ.IsHamiltonianVectorField (fun y ↦ G (y, t)) (Φ.velocity t)

/-- Unfolding `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.IsGeneratedBy`. -/
theorem isGeneratedBy_iff : Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ G ↔ ContMDiff (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ G ∧
    ∀ t, σ.IsHamiltonianVectorField (fun y ↦ G (y, t)) (Φ.velocity t) :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- A generating function of a diffeotopy is smooth. -/
theorem IsGeneratedBy.contMDiff (h : Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ G) :
    ContMDiff (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ G :=
  h.1

/-- If `G` generates `φ_t`, then `X_t` is a Hamiltonian vector field of `G_t`. -/
theorem IsGeneratedBy.isHamiltonianVectorField (h : Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ G) (t : unitInterval) :
    σ.IsHamiltonianVectorField (fun y ↦ G (y, t)) (Φ.velocity t) :=
  h.2 t

/-- For a closed two-form `σ`, every map `φ_t` of a diffeotopy generated by a function `G` on
`M × [0, 1]` preserves `σ`. -/
theorem IsGeneratedBy.timeSlice_mem_diffeomorphStabilizer [J.Boundaryless] (hσ : σ.IsClosed)
    (hΦ : Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ G) (t : unitInterval) :
    Φ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ :=
  (Φ.forall_timeSlice_mem_diffeomorphStabilizer_iff hσ).2 (fun u ↦
    SmoothTwoForm.mem_symplecticVectorFields_of_isHamiltonianVectorField
      (φ := ⟨RoughForm.ofFunction J fun y ↦ G (y, u), (isSmoothForm_ofFunction_iff.2
        (hΦ.contMDiff.comp (contMDiff_id.prodMk contMDiff_const))).mem_smoothBundleForms⟩)
      (by simpa only [RoughForm.ofFunction_apply, coe_smoothVelocity] using
        hΦ.isHamiltonianVectorField u)) t

/-- **Hamiltonians on `M` and along the motion.** For `G` on `M × [0, 1]`, the function
`(x, t) ↦ G (φ_t x, t)` is a Hamiltonian of `φ_t` read along the motion exactly when `G`
generates `φ_t`. Unlike Tau Ceti's
`TauCeti.Diffeotopy.hasHamiltonian_iff_isHamiltonianVectorField_velocity`, which it follows from,
it does not assume that `G` is smooth. -/
theorem hasHamiltonian_comp_iff :
    Φ.HasHamiltonian σ (fun p ↦ G (Φ.cylinderMap p, p.2)) ↔ Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ G := by
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ ?_, fun h ↦ (hasHamiltonian_iff_isHamiltonianVectorField_velocity h.1).2 h.2⟩
  have hG : ContMDiff (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ G := by
    refine (h.contMDiff.comp Φ.symm.contMDiff_cylinderMap_prodMk_snd).congr fun p ↦ ?_
    rw [Function.comp_apply, cylinderMap_apply, cylinderMap_apply, apply_mk_symm_apply]
  exact ⟨hG, (hasHamiltonian_iff_isHamiltonianVectorField_velocity hG).1 h⟩

/-- **The two readings of a Hamiltonian.** A function `F` on `M × [0, 1]` is a Hamiltonian of
`φ_t` read along the motion exactly when it is smooth and, for every `t`, the velocity `X_t` is a
Hamiltonian vector field of `H_t = F_t ∘ φ_t⁻¹`. -/
theorem hasHamiltonian_iff_contMDiff_and_isHamiltonianVectorField_velocity :
    Φ.HasHamiltonian σ F ↔ ContMDiff (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ F ∧
      ∀ t, σ.IsHamiltonianVectorField (fun y ↦ F (Φ.symm (t, y), t)) (Φ.velocity t) := by
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ ⟨h.contMDiff, fun t ↦ ?_⟩, fun ⟨hF, hX⟩ ↦ ?_⟩
  · simpa only [Function.comp_def, symm_timeSlice_apply] using
      h.isHamiltonianVectorField_velocity t
  · have hG : ContMDiff (J.prod (𝓡∂ 1)) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ fun p : M × unitInterval ↦
        F (Φ.symm (p.2, p.1), p.2) :=
      (hF.comp Φ.symm.contMDiff_cylinderMap_prodMk_snd).congr fun p ↦ by
        rw [Function.comp_apply, cylinderMap_apply]
    simpa only [cylinderMap_apply, symm_apply_mk_apply] using
      (hasHamiltonian_comp_iff (G := fun p ↦ F (Φ.symm (p.2, p.1), p.2))).2 ⟨hG, hX⟩

/-- **From a Hamiltonian along the motion to one on `M`.** If `F` is a Hamiltonian of `φ_t` read
along the motion, then `H_t = F_t ∘ φ_t⁻¹` generates `φ_t`. -/
theorem HasHamiltonian.isGeneratedBy (hF : Φ.HasHamiltonian σ F) :
    Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ fun p ↦ F (Φ.symm (p.2, p.1), p.2) :=
  hasHamiltonian_comp_iff.1 (by simpa only [cylinderMap_apply, symm_apply_mk_apply] using hF)

/-- For a closed two-form `σ` on a manifold without boundary, every map `φ_t` of a diffeotopy
with a Hamiltonian, read along the motion, preserves `σ`. -/
theorem HasHamiltonian.timeSlice_mem_diffeomorphStabilizer [J.Boundaryless] (hσ : σ.IsClosed)
    (hF : Φ.HasHamiltonian σ F) (t : unitInterval) :
    Φ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ :=
  hF.isGeneratedBy.timeSlice_mem_diffeomorphStabilizer hσ t

/-- A diffeotopy is Hamiltonian exactly when every slice preserves `σ` and some function on
`M × [0, 1]` generates it. -/
theorem isHamiltonian_iff_exists_isGeneratedBy : Φ.IsHamiltonian σ ↔
    (∀ t, Φ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) ∧ ∃ G, Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ G :=
  isHamiltonian_iff.trans (and_congr_right fun _ ↦ ⟨fun ⟨_, hF⟩ ↦ ⟨_, hF.isGeneratedBy⟩,
    fun ⟨_, hG⟩ ↦ ⟨_, hasHamiltonian_comp_iff.2 hG⟩⟩)

/-- For a closed two-form `σ` on a manifold without boundary, a diffeotopy generated by a function
on `M × [0, 1]` is Hamiltonian. -/
theorem IsGeneratedBy.isHamiltonian [J.Boundaryless] (hσ : σ.IsClosed)
    (hΦ : Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ G) : Φ.IsHamiltonian σ :=
  isHamiltonian_iff_exists_isGeneratedBy.2 ⟨hΦ.timeSlice_mem_diffeomorphStabilizer hσ, G, hΦ⟩

/-- The constant diffeotopy is generated by the zero function. -/
theorem isGeneratedBy_refl : (refl J ∞ M).IsGeneratedBy σ 0 :=
  hasHamiltonian_comp_iff.1 hasHamiltonian_refl

/-- **Hamiltonians of a composite diffeotopy, on `M`.** If `F` generates `φ_t`, `G` generates
`ψ_t` and every `φ_t` preserves `σ`, then `F_t + G_t ∘ φ_t⁻¹` generates the composite
`φ_t ∘ ψ_t`, which is `Ψ.trans Φ`. -/
theorem IsGeneratedBy.trans (hF : Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ F) (hG : Ψ.IsGeneratedBy σ G)
    (hΦ : ∀ t, Φ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) :
    (Ψ.trans Φ).IsGeneratedBy σ (fun p ↦ F p + G (Φ.symm (p.2, p.1), p.2)) := by
  rw [← hasHamiltonian_comp_iff]
  convert (hasHamiltonian_comp_iff.2 hG).trans (hasHamiltonian_comp_iff.2 hF) hΦ using 2 with p
  rw [cylinderMap_apply, cylinderMap_apply, trans_apply, cylinderMap_apply, symm_apply_mk_apply]

/-- **Hamiltonians of the inverse diffeotopy, on `M`.** If `F` generates `φ_t` and every `φ_t`
preserves `σ`, then `-F_t ∘ φ_t` generates the inverse diffeotopy `φ_t⁻¹`. -/
theorem IsGeneratedBy.symm (hF : Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ F)
    (hΦ : ∀ t, Φ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) :
    Φ.symm.IsGeneratedBy σ (fun p ↦ -F (Φ.cylinderMap p, p.2)) :=
  hasHamiltonian_comp_iff.1 ((hasHamiltonian_comp_iff.2 hF).symm hΦ)

/-- **Naturality of generating functions.** If `F` generates `φ_t` and the diffeomorphism `χ`
preserves `σ`, then `F_t ∘ χ` generates the conjugate `χ⁻¹ ∘ φ_t ∘ χ`, which is
`Φ.transDiffeomorph χ.symm`. -/
theorem IsGeneratedBy.transDiffeomorph {χ : M ≃ₘ⟮J, J⟯ M}
    (hχ : χ ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) (hF : Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ F) :
    (Φ.transDiffeomorph χ.symm).IsGeneratedBy σ (fun p ↦ F (χ p.1, p.2)) := by
  have hχ' : χ.symm ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ := Diffeomorph.inv_def χ ▸ inv_mem hχ
  rw [← hasHamiltonian_comp_iff]
  convert HasHamiltonian.transDiffeomorph (σ := σ) χ.symm
    (F := fun q ↦ F (Φ.cylinderMap q, q.2))
    (by rw [SmoothForm.mem_diffeomorphStabilizer.1 hχ']; exact hasHamiltonian_comp_iff.2 hF)
    using 2 with p
  simp

/-- **Uniqueness of generating functions.** Two functions that generate the same diffeotopy differ
on every connected component of `M` by a smooth function of `t` alone. -/
theorem IsGeneratedBy.exists_sub_eq (hF : Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ F) (hG : Φ.IsGeneratedBy σ G) :
    ∃ c : ConnectedComponents M → unitInterval → ℝ,
      (∀ i, ContMDiff (𝓡∂ 1) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ (c i)) ∧
        ∀ p, F p - G p = c (ConnectedComponents.mk p.1) p.2 := by
  have hloc (t : unitInterval) : IsLocallyConstant fun y ↦ F (y, t) - G (y, t) := by
    have hf : ContMDiff J 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ fun y ↦ F (y, t) :=
      hF.contMDiff.comp (contMDiff_id.prodMk contMDiff_const)
    have hg : ContMDiff J 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ fun y ↦ G (y, t) :=
      hG.contMDiff.comp (contMDiff_id.prodMk contMDiff_const)
    have h := (hF.isHamiltonianVectorField t).sub (hG.isHamiltonianVectorField t)
      (hf.mdifferentiable (by simp)) (hg.mdifferentiable (by simp))
    rw [sub_self] at h
    exact ((hf.sub hg).mdifferentiable (by simp)).isLocallyConstant_of_mfderiv_eq_zero
      fun y ↦ mvfderiv_eq_zero_iff.1 (SmoothTwoForm.isHamiltonianVectorField_zero_iff.1 h y)
  let r := Function.surjInv (ConnectedComponents.surjective_coe (α := M))
  refine ⟨fun i t ↦ F (r i, t) - G (r i, t), fun i ↦ ?_, fun p ↦ ?_⟩
  · exact (hF.contMDiff.comp (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id)).sub
      (hG.contMDiff.comp (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id))
  · have hr : r (ConnectedComponents.mk p.1) ∈ connectedComponent p.1 :=
      ConnectedComponents.coe_eq_coe'.1 (Function.surjInv_eq _ _)
    exact (hloc p.2).apply_eq_of_isPreconnected isPreconnected_connectedComponent
      mem_connectedComponent hr

/-- **Uniqueness of Hamiltonians.** Two Hamiltonians of the same diffeotopy, read along the
motion, differ on every connected component of `M` by a smooth function of `t` alone. -/
theorem HasHamiltonian.exists_sub_eq (hF : Φ.HasHamiltonian σ F) (hG : Φ.HasHamiltonian σ G) :
    ∃ c : ConnectedComponents M → unitInterval → ℝ,
      (∀ i, ContMDiff (𝓡∂ 1) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ (c i)) ∧
        ∀ p, F p - G p = c (ConnectedComponents.mk p.1) p.2 := by
  obtain ⟨c, hc, hFG⟩ := hF.isGeneratedBy.exists_sub_eq hG.isGeneratedBy
  refine ⟨c, hc, fun p ↦ ?_⟩
  simpa only [symm_apply_mk_apply,
    ConnectedComponents.coe_eq_coe.2 (Φ.connectedComponent_apply (p.2, p.1))] using
    hFG (Φ (p.2, p.1), p.2)


/-! ### Hamiltonians from exactness -/

/-- **A diffeotopy has a Hamiltonian when its velocity forms are exact.** If, for every `t`, the
contraction `ι_{X_t} σ` of `σ` with the velocity of `φ_t` is exact, then `φ_t` has a
Hamiltonian, read along the motion. Neither closedness nor nondegeneracy of `σ` is needed. -/
theorem exists_hasHamiltonian_of_forall_mem_exactForms
    (h : ∀ t, σ.interiorₗ (Φ.smoothVelocity t) ∈ exactForms J M 1) : ∃ F, Φ.HasHamiltonian σ F := by
  refine exists_hasHamiltonian_iff.2 fun t ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨f, hf, hdf⟩ := exists_contMDiff_mextDeriv_eq_of_mem_exactForms J (h t)
  refine ⟨f, hf.mdifferentiable (by simp), ?_⟩
  rw [SmoothTwoForm.isHamiltonianVectorField_iff_interior_eq, ← coe_smoothVelocity,
    ← SmoothTwoForm.coe_interiorₗ]
  exact hdf.symm

/-- **Hamiltonians and exactness.** A diffeotopy `φ_t` has a Hamiltonian, read along the motion,
exactly when, for every `t`, the contraction `ι_{X_t} σ` of `σ` with its velocity is exact. This
is Tau Ceti's `TauCeti.Diffeotopy.exists_hasHamiltonian_iff` with exactness in place of a
differentiable Hamiltonian function at each time. -/
theorem exists_hasHamiltonian_iff_forall_interiorₗ_velocity_mem_exactForms :
    (∃ F, Φ.HasHamiltonian σ F) ↔ ∀ t, σ.interiorₗ (Φ.smoothVelocity t) ∈ exactForms J M 1 := by
  refine ⟨fun ⟨F, hF⟩ t ↦ ?_, exists_hasHamiltonian_of_forall_mem_exactForms⟩
  obtain ⟨hFs, hX⟩ := hasHamiltonian_iff_contMDiff_and_isHamiltonianVectorField_velocity.1 hF
  have hs : ContMDiff J 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ fun y ↦ F (Φ.symm (t, y), t) :=
    hFs.comp ((Φ.symm.contMDiff.comp (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id)).prodMk
      contMDiff_const)
  rw [exactForms_succ]
  exact ⟨⟨_, (isSmoothForm_ofFunction_iff.2 hs).mem_smoothBundleForms⟩,
    (SmoothTwoForm.isHamiltonianVectorField_iff_interiorₗ_eq.1 (by simpa using hX t)).symm⟩

/-- **Hamiltonian diffeotopies and exactness.** A diffeotopy `φ_t` all of whose slices preserve
`σ` is Hamiltonian exactly when, for every `t`, the contraction `ι_{X_t} σ` of `σ` with its
velocity is exact. -/
theorem isHamiltonian_iff_forall_interiorₗ_velocity_mem_exactForms
    (hΦ : ∀ t, Φ.timeSlice t ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer σ) :
    Φ.IsHamiltonian σ ↔ ∀ t, σ.interiorₗ (Φ.smoothVelocity t) ∈ exactForms J M 1 := by
  rw [isHamiltonian_iff, ← exists_hasHamiltonian_iff_forall_interiorₗ_velocity_mem_exactForms]
  exact and_iff_right hΦ

/-- For a Hamiltonian diffeotopy `φ_t` of `σ`, the contraction `ι_{X_t} σ` of `σ` with the
velocity `X_t` is exact for every `t`. -/
theorem IsHamiltonian.interiorₗ_velocity_mem_exactForms (hΦ : Φ.IsHamiltonian σ)
    (t : unitInterval) : σ.interiorₗ (Φ.smoothVelocity t) ∈ exactForms J M 1 :=
  (isHamiltonian_iff_forall_interiorₗ_velocity_mem_exactForms
    hΦ.timeSlice_mem_diffeomorphStabilizer).1 hΦ t

/-- For a Hamiltonian diffeotopy `φ_t` of `σ` and every time `t`, the line integral from `0` to
`1` of `ι_{X_t} σ` along a `C¹` curve `c` with `c 0 = c 1` vanishes. -/
theorem IsHamiltonian.pathIntegral_interiorₗ_velocity_eq_zero (hΦ : Φ.IsHamiltonian σ)
    (t : unitInterval) {c : ℝ → M} (hc : ContMDiff 𝓘(ℝ, ℝ) J 1 c) (hc₀₁ : c 0 = c 1) :
    pathIntegral (σ.interiorₗ (Φ.smoothVelocity t)).val c 0 1 = 0 :=
  pathIntegral_eq_zero_of_mem_exactForms (hΦ.interiorₗ_velocity_mem_exactForms t) hc hc₀₁

/-- The flux of a diffeotopy depends only on the diffeotopy: equal diffeotopies have equal fluxes,
whichever proofs that their final maps preserve `τ` are given. -/
theorem flux_congr {τ : closedForms J M 2} (e : Φ = Ψ)
    (hΦ : Φ.final ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer τ.val)
    (hΨ : Ψ.final ∈ SmoothForm.diffeomorphStabilizer τ.val) : Φ.flux τ hΦ = Ψ.flux τ hΨ := by
  subst e
  rfl

end TauCeti.Diffeotopy

end
